{"id":"int-ba82141886290c5506c80bc50a4120c7","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-06T11:27:54.558761Z","actor":"Dariusz Debowczyk","issue_id":"instructor-a214.6","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"R4 delivered the concrete piece: per-example recording namespaces. HttpRecordingBoot::withExampleNamespace derives <root>/<Group>/<Example> from the run.php SCRIPT_FILENAME -> refresh is scoped to one folder, cross-example collisions impossible. Verified e2e (recording lands under A05_Extras/ComplexExtractionGemini/, replay stable) + 3 derivation branches (example/non-example/empty). Canonical-JSON matcher DEFERRED with evidence: no corpus example has a non-deterministic request body (json_encode is stable; R0/R1b proved byte-stable replay under ExactHashMatcher). The RequestMatcher contract from R1a is the ready seam - add CanonicalJsonMatcher when a real drift case appears (R5 would surface it)."}}
{"id":"int-e279989028f1cf3cb13afa7924a8464f","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-06T11:27:54.846956Z","actor":"Dariusz Debowczyk","issue_id":"instructor-a214.5","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"DEFERRED - no consumer in the current corpus. R3 solves byte-IDENTICAL requests sent twice expecting different responses (network-level transient retry). Evidence: the corpus 'retry' examples (SelfCorrection, ValidationWithLLM, ValidationCustom, ToolUse, etc.) are VALIDATION-driven - each retry sends an AUGMENTED request with error feedback -> different body -> different fingerprint -> distinct recording under the existing one-file-per-fingerprint model. No example issues an identical request twice. The RequestMatcher/storage design supports ordered cassettes when a real consumer appears; reopen then. Not building speculatively (stepping-stones: experiment over speculation)."}}
